WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.460
One of the great
challenges in this world

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.620
is knowing enough
about a subject

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:10.670
to think you're right but
not enough about the subject

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:11.885
to know you're wrong.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:18.700
There's like a gazillion
hours of me on the internet.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.320
In almost every case, I'm
talking about the universe--

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.680
black holes, the big
bang, time travel, God.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.020
What I'm going to do
in this MasterClass

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.960
is teach you how to think.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.170
The goal here is
to train your mind

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.240
how to see the world
differently, how

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.510
to question what others say.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:42.640
I've come to realize that there
are three categories of truth--

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.200
personal truth,
political truths,

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.010
and the objective truths
that shape our understanding

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:49.243
of the universe.

00:00:49.243 --> 00:00:51.160
The interesting thing
about an objective truth

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.190
is that it's true
no matter what.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.170
Imagine that.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.570
By the time we're
done, you will be

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:01.270
equipped with some of
the methods and tools

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:04.930
so you can turn data into
information, information

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:09.890
into knowledge,
knowledge into wisdom.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:16.040
We all have
susceptibility to bias.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:21.290
Search engines on the internet
are the epitome of confirmation

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:23.750
bias, and you're going
to use that as evidence

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.650
that you are correct?

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.030
No.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:30.360
The good thing about science is
that it's true whether or not

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.230
you believe in it.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:32.780
What does it mean
to be skeptical?

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.530
What does it mean to
be convinced by data?

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.740
A proper skeptic questions
what they're unsure

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.440
of but recognizes
when valid evidence is

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:44.200
presented to change their mind.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.860
I will equip you to not
only find objective truths

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:51.350
but then communicate to
others how to get there.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.760
It's not good
enough to be right.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.210
You also have to be effective.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:58.570
The less connected you are
to what is objectively true,

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:02.140
the less likely you will
be able to make decisions

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.060
that will benefit your life--

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.540
your life, the life of your
family, and even civilization

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:09.250
itself.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:14.580
I'm Neil deGrasse Tyson,
and this is my MasterClass.

